   "notes": "The article's EOS fits use cubic volumes for all 17 helium rows, cubic volumes for the first five neon rows through 19.244 GPa, and hexagonal volumes for the seven neon rows from 24.084 GPa onward. The source also reports the unused alternate indexing at every pressure, retained here without cleaning. At 31.820 GPa helium, ruby 1 was estimated from ruby 2 using P_ruby1=0.9973 P_ruby2+1.8804 GPa because its wavelength was not measured. The official workbook omits a closing parenthesis in two 16.199(65) cells; the visually typeset official PDF confirms 16.199(65), which is transcribed here. The ambient footnote gives the geometric cubic-to-hexagonal transformation a_hex=a_cubic/sqrt(2), c_hex=sqrt(3)a_cubic, V_hex=3V_cubic/4."
